WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.000
-The Weirdos. Thank you guys

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.033
so much for being here.

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:06.767
Chris, we know each other --
-Yes. I love you.

00:00:06.767 --> 00:00:08.501
-I love you, too --
for a long time.

00:00:08.501 --> 00:00:10.234
[ Laughter ]
But can The Weirdos quickly

00:00:10.234 --> 00:00:11.400
introduce themselves?

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.467
-[ English accent ]
Yeah, right, I'm Donk

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:15.901
and, believe it or not,
I'm the normal one.

00:00:15.901 --> 00:00:18.133
-Oh, my gosh.
-Except, I play drums.

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:20.868
-Ah, the drummer, Dunk, yes.

00:00:20.868 --> 00:00:23.267
-My name is The Wizard,
but I'm not --

00:00:23.267 --> 00:00:25.901
I'm not that kind of wizard.

00:00:25.901 --> 00:00:29.501
I'm -- I'm the kind of guy
who just is super smart

00:00:29.501 --> 00:00:31.767
and -- and I do magic.

00:00:31.767 --> 00:00:33.033
-Like a normal --
like a wizard.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.267
-That is what a wizard --
-Yeah, yeah,

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:35.868
-That's a wizard, mate.
-Like a normal wizard.

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:37.200
Yeah.
-Okay, okay, yes.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.334
-And you, right here,
very beautiful.

00:00:39.334 --> 00:00:42.100
-My name is Angel Moon.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.801
I'm a singer.

00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:47.200
I'm 109 light-years old.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:49.467
-Wow!
-How old are you, Jimmy?

00:00:49.467 --> 00:00:50.934
You're gorgeous.

00:00:50.934 --> 00:00:53.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:53.534 --> 00:00:55.400
-That's really kind of creepy.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.801
-I like that, no. Oh, my gosh.
Thank you very much.

00:00:57.801 --> 00:01:01.467
I'm much, much older than that.

00:01:01.467 --> 00:01:02.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.868 --> 00:01:05.400
How about back there?
-♪ Sparkman ♪

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:08.133
♪ I play guitar ♪

00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:09.801
[ Laughter ]
-Sparkman.

00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:11.601
You play guitar, but it's weird.

00:01:11.601 --> 00:01:13.801
Do you sing as well,
in the band?

00:01:13.801 --> 00:01:16.067
-♪ No, I don't like to sing ♪

00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:18.834
[ Laughter ]
-No, he plays the guitar.

00:01:18.834 --> 00:01:20.567
-Yeah, but you have
a beautiful voice.

00:01:20.567 --> 00:01:22.467
Maybe you should try singing.

00:01:22.467 --> 00:01:23.467
-♪ Mm ♪

00:01:23.467 --> 00:01:24.667
♪ Not for me ♪

00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:26.667
[ Laughter ]
♪ I'm too shy ♪

00:01:26.667 --> 00:01:28.968
-♪ You're too shy, of course ♪
-He's very shy.

00:01:28.968 --> 00:01:31.200
-But your manager
is here tonight as well.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.400
Can we get a shot
of your manager?

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:36.100
[ Laughter and applause ]
Bruce, Bruce Cakemix is here.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:37.667
-Whoa, whoa, no, Jimmy --
-Well, thank you for being here.

00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:40.767
Jimmy, no.
-No, not Cakemix.

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:43.400
"Kehkehmix."

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:47.701
He gets very angry
if you call him Mr. Cakemix.

00:01:47.701 --> 00:01:51.334
-I'm sorry. Bruce Kehkehmix?
-Spelled like Cakemix,

00:01:51.334 --> 00:01:53.300
but it's pronounced Kehkehmix.

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:54.267
[ Laughter ]
-Don't make him angry.

00:01:54.267 --> 00:01:55.734
You won't like him
when he's angry.

00:01:55.734 --> 00:01:56.934
-Yeah, you won't like it.

00:01:56.934 --> 00:01:59.534
-That man in a sweater vest
will get angry?

00:01:59.534 --> 00:02:01.000
-Yeah.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.234 --> 00:02:04.167
-Yeah.
This is the first time

00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:07.567
we've had a band on
from another planet.

00:02:07.567 --> 00:02:10.200
Donk, what planet are you from?

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.167
-Well, it's really hard
to pronounce,

00:02:12.167 --> 00:02:14.534
so we just call it Melissa.

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:15.667
[ Laughter ]
-Wow.

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:17.601
And, on Melissa,

00:02:17.601 --> 00:02:19.234
do you get
"The Tonight Show" there?

00:02:19.234 --> 00:02:21.934
-Well, yeah, but,

00:02:21.934 --> 00:02:23.467
you see,
you've broadcast it a while

00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:24.834
and it takes a long time

00:02:24.834 --> 00:02:27.167
for transmissions
to reach our planet.

00:02:27.167 --> 00:02:28.901
-Is there a time delay
where they're from?

00:02:28.901 --> 00:02:30.400
-Yeah.
-Yeah, back on our planet,

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:31.868
you're still riding
around in a yellow cab

00:02:31.868 --> 00:02:33.167
with Queen Latifah.

00:02:33.167 --> 00:02:34.300
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah!

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:37.133
That was a good jam.
I remember that one.

00:02:37.133 --> 00:02:41.267
Angel Moon, what's your favorite
thing about Earth, so far?

00:02:41.267 --> 00:02:45.868
-My favorite thing
about Earth is

00:02:45.868 --> 00:02:48.868
probably you.

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:49.934
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:49.934 --> 00:02:51.367
♪ Is you, Jimmy ♪
-I'm just in --

00:02:51.367 --> 00:02:53.033
I'm in love.
-Wait, wait.

00:02:53.033 --> 00:02:57.067
-♪ All I think about is you ♪

00:02:57.067 --> 00:02:58.434
♪ Jimmy ♪

00:02:58.434 --> 00:03:01.667
[ Laughter and applause ]
♪ It's all that I can do ♪

00:03:01.667 --> 00:03:03.334
♪ Every day ♪

00:03:03.334 --> 00:03:06.667
♪ When I'm dreaming away ♪

00:03:06.667 --> 00:03:09.334
♪ About you ♪

00:03:09.334 --> 00:03:11.200
♪ Jimmy, Jimmy ♪

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:12.667
♪ J ♪

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:13.801
♪ For Jimmy ♪

00:03:13.801 --> 00:03:15.467
-J for Jimmy.
-Wow, my God!

00:03:15.467 --> 00:03:17.167
Angel Moon, that was the most
beautiful...

00:03:17.167 --> 00:03:18.467
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Yeah!

00:03:18.467 --> 00:03:22.434
-...beautiful
voice I've ever heard.

00:03:22.434 --> 00:03:24.734
It's really, Chris,
she has an amazing voice.

00:03:24.734 --> 00:03:27.000
-She has an amazing voice.
-She does.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.667
-She really --
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:28.667 --> 00:03:30.267
-She really -- You really do.

00:03:30.267 --> 00:03:31.868
-Chris, you're a big fan
of The Weirdos

00:03:31.868 --> 00:03:33.400
and you've been wanting to work
with them for a while.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.601
-Yeah.
-How did you finally meet?

00:03:35.601 --> 00:03:38.067
-Well, the rest of the band,
Coldplay, and I,

00:03:38.067 --> 00:03:40.000
we went to --
we were lucky enough

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.601
to get tickets
to see them in concert

00:03:41.601 --> 00:03:44.634
and we just tried to get
their attention, to say,

00:03:44.634 --> 00:03:46.901
"Please, one day,
could we work together?"

00:03:46.901 --> 00:03:48.868
[ Laughter ]
And...
-Yeah.

00:03:48.868 --> 00:03:51.501
-We have a clip, actually,
of the moment that we met.

00:03:51.501 --> 00:03:53.167
-Of Coldplay
at a Weirdos concert?

00:03:53.167 --> 00:03:55.634
-Yeah, because we love to go see
things together and --

00:03:55.634 --> 00:03:57.367
-As a band, yeah.

00:03:57.367 --> 00:03:59.200
You and Coldplay,
you and the band just travel.

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:00.868
You do everything together.
-Everything.

00:04:00.868 --> 00:04:03.767
[ Laughter ]
And we'd just finished at a nail
spa together and we went

00:04:03.767 --> 00:04:05.100
[ Laughter ]
to see.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:06.300
-You were getting mani-pedis

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:07.801
and then you went
to the Weirdos concert.

00:04:07.801 --> 00:04:09.701
-Exactly.
-And we have a video.

00:04:09.701 --> 00:04:11.467
Check this out.
-This is how we met.

00:04:11.467 --> 00:04:14.834
-♪ So biutyful ♪

00:04:14.834 --> 00:04:17.634
♪♪

00:04:17.634 --> 00:04:20.167
♪ Yes, you're biutyful ♪

00:04:20.167 --> 00:04:21.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:23.868
♪♪

00:04:23.868 --> 00:04:25.567
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Wow. That's amazing.

00:04:25.567 --> 00:04:28.501
-Yeah.
-I see it now, yeah.

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:32.434
Now, Angel Moon,
gosh, you are very beautiful,

00:04:32.434 --> 00:04:33.567
so it goes with the song,

00:04:33.567 --> 00:04:36.467
but tell us about the new song.
-Ooh!

00:04:36.467 --> 00:04:40.300
Jimmy, the song "Biutyful"

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:45.634
is spelled differently
where we come from,

00:04:45.634 --> 00:04:50.234
but, really, the song is
about how

00:04:50.234 --> 00:04:53.834
there is beauty and magic

00:04:53.834 --> 00:04:57.767
in all things and all people.

00:04:57.767 --> 00:04:58.968
-Yeah, I agree.

00:04:58.968 --> 00:05:00.267
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:00.267 --> 00:05:02.267
-Is that what it meant?
-That's it. [ Laughs ]

00:05:02.267 --> 00:05:03.701
-That's what it's about.
-That's what it's about.

00:05:03.701 --> 00:05:05.767
-Weirdos, I wanted to thank you,
again, for being here

00:05:05.767 --> 00:05:07.934
and you're going to perform
for us tonight.

00:05:07.934 --> 00:05:09.100
I really appreciate this.

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:11.267
And a big New York City welcome.

00:05:11.267 --> 00:05:12.467
-Thank you, Jimmy.

00:05:12.467 --> 00:05:14.267
We love you so much.

00:05:14.267 --> 00:05:15.968
This is the best day

00:05:15.968 --> 00:05:18.901
♪ Of my life ♪

00:05:18.901 --> 00:05:20.934
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Oh, my.

00:05:20.934 --> 00:05:23.100
I love you guys.
The Weirdos,

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:25.667
featuring Chris Martin
of Coldplay, everybody.

00:05:25.667 --> 00:05:28.367
Catch them on the
Music of the Spheres World Tour

00:05:28.367 --> 00:05:30.968
and they're performing for us
later on the show.

